---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import SpinnerDemo from "../../components/SpinnerDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Spinner"
  description="A small spinning loader for buttons, status lines, and icon slots, and a thought orb for AI work."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Spinner</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Shows that something is working when you cannot show its shape. Use it in
    busy buttons, short status lines, and in place of a status icon while a step
    runs. To hold the space of content that is loading, use Skeleton.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><SpinnerDemo client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Spinner usage"
      code={`import { Spinner } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/spinner";

<p role="status" className="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-sprout-muted">
  <Spinner aria-hidden="true" />
  Loading rows…
</p>

<Badge variant="secondary">
  <Spinner size="sm" aria-hidden="true" />
  Finding sources
</Badge>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>Spinner</code> renders an SVG that takes the current text color.
      <code>size</code> sets its size:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>"sm"</code>: 12px, for badges.</li>
      <li>
        <code>"default"</code>: 16px, for text rows and buttons. Buttons of
        every size keep it at 16px.
      </li>
      <li><code>"lg"</code>: 20px, to swap with 20px status icons.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <code>className</code>, <code>style</code>, <code>data-*</code>, and other
      SVG attributes pass through.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Thinking</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Thought orb for AI and agent work"
      code={`<p role="status" className="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm">
  <Spinner variant="thinking" activity="searching" aria-hidden="true" />
  Searching your Drive…
</p>

<Spinner variant="thinking" size="xl" activity="composing" aria-label="Writing a reply" />`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>variant="thinking"</code> draws a dotted orb from
      <a href="https://github.com/Jakubantalik/thinking-orbs">thinking-orbs</a>
      (MIT) on a canvas. <code>activity</code> picks one of nine animations:
      <code>working</code> (default), <code>searching</code>,
      <code>solving</code>, <code>listening</code>, <code>connecting</code>,
      <code>weaving</code>, <code>composing</code>, <code>breathing</code>, and <code
        >shaping</code
      >. <code>spinnerActivityNames</code> lists them.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>"lg"</code>: 20px, the default, beside text.</li>
      <li><code>"xl"</code>: 64px, at avatar scale.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The two sizes are separately tuned designs, so the orb has no
      <code>"sm"</code> or <code>"default"</code>. Its code loads the first time
      a thinking spinner renders, so apps that only use the loader never
      download it. The orb is monochrome: dark dots on light themes and light
      dots on dark themes, following the <code>dark</code> and
      <code>light</code> classes or the system setting. It does not take the text
      color. With reduced motion it shows a still frame.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Busy buttons</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Leading spinner with a pending label"
      code={`<Button disabled={pending} aria-busy={pending} onClick={begin}>
  {pending && <Spinner aria-hidden="true" />}
  {pending ? "Opening sign-in…" : "Connect account"}
</Button>

<Button disabled={saving} aria-busy={saving}>
  {saving ? <Spinner aria-hidden="true" /> : <ArrowRight aria-hidden="true" />}
  {saving ? "Creating workspace…" : "Create workspace"}
</Button>`}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Status icons</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Swap with a 20px icon"
      code={`<span className="size-5">
  {busy ? <Spinner size="lg" aria-hidden="true" /> : <Database size={20} aria-hidden="true" />}
</span>`}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      By default the spinner has <code>role="status"</code> and the name “Loading”,
      or “Thinking” for <code>variant="thinking"</code>. Pass <code
        >aria-label</code
      >, such as “Opening workspace”, when the spinner stands alone. When text
      beside it already explains the wait, pass <code>aria-hidden="true"</code>:
      the role and name are then left out, and the sentence’s own status region
      is read instead.
    </p>
    <p>
      The spinner turns once a second and stops when reduced motion is
      requested. Its fading spokes still read as loading when still. It is never
      focusable and ignores the pointer.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      The spinner has no color of its own. It uses <code>currentColor</code>, so
      it follows the text, button, or badge it sits in, in light, dark, and
      brand themes.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
